# V2 components → Storybook

When creating or updating a **v2** UI component (anything under a `v2/` folder intended for reuse), also add or update a colocated Storybook story.

## Requirements

- Place stories next to the component: `ComponentName.stories.tsx`
- Use CSF3 with `title` under the `v2/` group, e.g. `v2/Button`, `v2/LinkButton`
- Include `tags: ['autodocs']`
- Cover the main variants, sizes, and disabled state that the design defines
- Rely on the global theme decorator in `.storybook/preview.tsx` (light/dark toolbar) — do not wrap stories in a second `ThemeProvider` unless the component needs something extra
- If the component uses React Router (`Link`, `useNavigate`, etc.), wrap that story file in `MemoryRouter`

## Example

```tsx
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/react-vite';
import { Button } from './index';

const meta = {
  title: 'v2/Button',
  component: Button,
  tags: ['autodocs'],
  args: { text: 'Button text', variant: 'primary' },
} satisfies Meta<typeof Button>;

export default meta;
type Story = StoryObj<typeof meta>;

export const Primary: Story = {};
```

## Out of scope

- Do not add stories for one-off container pages unless asked
- Legacy (non-v2) components do not need stories by default
